  "output": "Here is the full performance analysis across all five dimensions:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: cworkplace\n\n---\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n\n**Critical — `apps/api/src/server/notify.ts:27`**\n\nEvery notification is inserted individually in a loop. With 50 @-mentions in a post, that's 50 sequential INSERTs.\n\n```typescript\n// Current\nfor (const row of rows) await db.notification.create({ data: row });\n\n// Fix\nawait db.notification.createMany({ data: rows });\n```\n\n---\n\n**Critical — `apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:227–233`**\n\n`callTitle()` calls `db.event.findUnique()` or `db.conversation.findUnique()` **per invitee** inside a loop. With 6 participants, that's 6 identical DB queries for the same row.\n\n```typescript\n// Current\nfor (const userId of await invitees(call, user.id)) {\n  emitToUsers([userId], \"call:incoming\", {\n    title: await callTitle(call, userId), // ← re-queried for each\n  });\n}\n\n// Fix: hoist the title out of the loop\nconst title = await callTitle(call, user.id);\nfor (const userId of await invitees(call, user.id)) {\n  emitToUsers([userId], \"call:incoming\", { title });\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**High — `apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts` (multiple locations)**\n\nNearly every loop in the realtime plugin has an N+1:\n\n| Lines | Pattern | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 94–104 | Post lookup per comment | Batch with `findMany({ where: { id: { in: postIds } } })` |\n| 127–130 | Parent comment lookup per reply | Batch before loop |\n| 148–157 | Post lookup per reaction | Batch by `postId` |\n| 166–176 | `notification.findFirst` per reaction (2×) | Batch with `findMany`, index by key |\n| 243–256 | Group + admin queries per `GroupMember` row | Batch; cache admin list by `groupId` |\n| 294–306 | `conversationMemberIds()` per message | Group messages by `conversationId`, query once per conversation |\n| 317–330 | Message + member lookup per `MessageReaction` | Double batch: messages first, then members grouped by conversation |\n| 379–382 | `EventAttendee.findMany` per event | Batch: `findMany({ where: { eventId: { in: eventIds } } })` |\n| 391–400 | Event lookup per attendee row | Batch by `eventId` |\n\n---\n\n**Missing DB indexes** (inferred from query patterns in `schema.zmodel`):\n\n```\n@@index([postId, userId, actorId, type, readAt])  // on Notification — POST_REACTION dedup query\n@@index([groupId, userId, type])                  // on Notification — GROUP_JOIN queries\n@@index([eventId])                                 // on EventAttendee\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Unnecessary Re-renders\n\n**High — Context value objects created inline**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/ui/chart.tsx:62` — new object on every render, all `useChart()` consumers re-render:\n\n```tsx\n// Current\n<ChartContext.Provider value={{ config }}>\n\n// Fix\nconst value = React.useMemo(() => ({ config }), [config]);\n<ChartContext.Provider value={value}>\n```\n\n`apps/web/src/components/call/call-provider.tsx:133` — same problem, affects all call UI:\n\n```tsx\n// Current\n<CallsContext.Provider value={{ startCall, joinCall }}>\n\n// Fix\nconst value = React.useMemo(() => ({ startCall, joinCall }), [startCall, joinCall]);\n<CallsContext.Provider value={value}>\n```\n\n---\n\n**Medium — `org-layout.tsx:98–104`**\n\nThe `href` function is recreated on every render, making the entire `value` object new. Every `useOrg()` consumer re-renders when anything in `OrgLayout` changes:\n\n```tsx\n// Fix: wrap the value\nconst value = React.useMemo(() => ({\n  org,\n  me: session.user,\n  role,\n  isAdmin: role === \"owner\" || role === \"admin\",\n  href: (path = \"\") => `/${org.slug}${path === \"/\" ? \"\" : path}`,\n}), [org, session.user, role]);\n```\n\n---\n\n**Medium — filtering/sorting in render**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/settings/members-settings.tsx:108–115` — two `.filter()` calls with `.toLowerCase()` on every render:\n\n```tsx\n// Fix\nconst ownerCount = React.useMemo(\n  () => members.filter(m => m.role === \"owner\").length,\n  [members]\n);\nconst visible = React.useMemo(\n  () => members.filter(m => m.user.name.toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase())),\n  [members, q]\n);\n```\n\nSame pattern in:\n- `apps/web/src/components/settings/invitations-settings.tsx:161–164` (sort + two `getTime()` calls per render)\n- `apps/web/src/components/groups/group-members.tsx:110–117`\n- `apps/web/src/components/chat/conversation-list.tsx:49–66` (O(n²) — `.some()` inside `.filter()`)\n\n`apps/web/src/components/calendar/month-view.tsx:56–59` — O(days × occurrences) filter inside render loop — the worst offender in the calendar:\n\n```tsx\n// Fix: build a Map<dateKey, occurrence[]> with useMemo before rendering\nconst byDay = React.useMemo(() => {\n  const map = new Map<string, Occurrence[]>();\n  for (const occ of occurrences) {\n    const key = format(occ.start, \"yyyy-MM-dd\");\n    (map.get(key) ?? map.set(key, []).get(key)!).push(occ);\n  }\n  return map;\n}, [occurrences]);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n| What | Where | Suggested Cache |\n|---|---|---|\n| `callTitle()` result | `calls.ts:227` | In-memory per call ID, TTL = call lifetime |\n| `groupId → organizationId` | `realtime-plugin.ts:243` | In-memory Map, invalidate on group update |\n| Conversation member list | `realtime-plugin.ts:296, 337, 346` | In-memory Map, TTL 30–60 s, invalidate on `ConversationMember` change |\n| Admin/moderator list per group | `realtime-plugin.ts:249` | In-memory Map, invalidate on `GroupMember` role change |\n| POST_REACTION notification existence | `realtime-plugin.ts:166` | In-memory Set keyed by `(postId,userId,actorId)`, TTL 5 s |\n\nAll of these are hot paths that run for every realtime mutation. A simple `Map` with a TTL wrapper is enough — no Redis required since the spec mandates a single process.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**High — `apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:263–275`**\n\nThree `window`/`document` listeners registered in a `useEffect` with `[]` deps. If the component remounts, new listeners accumulate without removing the old ones. The cleanup is there but the dep array is wrong:\n\n```tsx\n// Current\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener(\"focus\", update);\n  window.addEventListener(\"blur\", update);\n  document.addEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", update);\n  return () => { /* removes current update */ };\n}, []);  // ← stale: won't re-register if update changes\n\n// Fix: add update to dependency array (ensure update is stable via useCallback)\n```\n\n---\n\n**Medium — `apps/web/src/components/call/media-elements.tsx:39–45`**\n\n`track.addEventListener(\"unmute\", onUnmute)` in a loop — `onUnmute` closes over `el` and `stream`, but if `stream` changes between renders, new listeners are added while old track references may not match, leaving orphaned listeners.\n\n---\n\n**Medium — `apps/web/src/hooks/use-socket.tsx:51–76`**\n\n`useSocketEvent` registers listeners on the socket instance. Verify the returned cleanup function calls `socket.off(event, handler)` — if the socket reference is stable but the component unmounts and remounts, listeners stack up.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**`packages/shared/src/mentions.ts:25–50`** — `matchAll()` runs two regex scans unconditionally on every text chunk, including plain text with no mentions or URLs:\n\n```typescript\n// Fix: early exit before expensive regex\nexport function parseText(text: string) {\n  const hasMention = text.includes(\"@\");\n  const hasUrl = text.includes(\"http\");\n  if (!hasMention && !hasUrl) return [{ type: \"text\", value: text }];\n  // ... existing matchAll logic\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:166–175`** — `sameGroup()` is defined inside the component body, recreated on every render, then called in a loop over every message:\n\n```tsx\n// Move outside component (pure function, no closure needed)\nfunction sameGroup(a: Message, b: Message) {\n  return a.senderId === b.senderId\n    && isSameDay(a.createdAt, b.createdAt)\n    && differenceInMinutes(b.createdAt, a.createdAt) < 5;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**`apps/api/src/routes/conversations.ts:14–35`** — two separate DB queries for the same conversation row (once through `userDb`, once through `db`) within a single request handler. Combine into one query or reuse the first result.\n\n---\n\n**`apps/api/src/lib/db.ts`** — the `pg.Pool` is created with no explicit config, meaning the default of `max: 10` connections applies. With realtime plugin handlers spawning multiple nested queries per event, pool exhaustion under load is likely:\n\n```typescript\npool: new Pool({\n  connectionString: env.DATABASE_URL,\n  max: 20,\n  idleTimeoutMillis: 30_000,\n  connectionTimeoutMillis: 5_000,\n}),\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Priority | Fix | File | Expected Gain |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P0 | `notify.ts`: loop → `createMany` | `server/notify.ts:27` | 50–100× on bulk notifications |\n| P0 | `callTitle()` outside invitee loop | `websocket/calls.ts:227` | Eliminates N×1 on every call start |\n| P1 | Batch post/comment/reaction queries in realtime plugin | `server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts` | Major DB load reduction |\n| P1 | Memoize context values in `chart.tsx` and `call-provider.tsx` | Multiple | Stops broad subtree re-renders |\n| P2 | Memoize `org-layout.tsx` value | `layout/org-layout.tsx:98` | Stops entire org layout from re-rendering |\n| P2 | Memoize filter/sort in settings + calendar | Multiple | Prevents O(n) work per keystroke/render |\n| P2 | `members-settings.tsx` and `month-view.tsx` useMemo | Settings + Calendar | CPU savings on large datasets |\n| P3 | Add 3 missing DB indexes | `schema.zmodel` | Faster notification dedup queries |\n| P3 | Fix window listener dep array in `message-list.tsx` | Chat | Eliminates listener leak |\n| P3 | Mention `parseText` early exit | `packages/shared` | Small but touches every message |\n| P3 | Pool size config | `lib/db.ts` | Prevents pool exhaustion under load |\n",
